{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1159771-magical-items-with-flaws","id":1159771,"title":"Magical items with flaws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-17T04:09:25-08:00","id":1159771,"title":"Magical items with flaws","content":"When creating Hunter endowments you can give them flaws in return for greater power. Can something similar be done with the imbued items and Artifacts in Mage? I feel like magical items with some sinister drawbacks can only be more juicy and flavourful for the game, such as a Mirror of happy memories that risks addicting you to it or a ring with Life spells that drinks your blood (costs you Health) with every use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:00:30-08:00","id":1159851,"title":"","content":"There are no mechanics for this in 2e, as far as I'm aware of it. But reasonably cursed items have been around in 1e and make sense. But you'll have to wing mechanics for their purchase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"